    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1233">

                <pb facs="1794" n="1778" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890H.51/9–1949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-19T14:00:00+04:30">September 19,
                            1949—2 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>217. Recent talks with Majid<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1233-f1"/> Minister of
                    National Economy confirms Embassy belief that loan urgently needed and
                    economically sound. US goodwill being jeopardized by what appears to Afghans as
                    unreasonable delay in considering loan. Present widespread criticism of
                        MK<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1233-f2"/> and American efficiency voiced by Majid
                    seriously undermining US prestige. For approximately $20,000,000 spent only
                    tangible returns Afghanistan has are one short road, one diversion dam and one
                    incomplete canal.</p>
                <p>Justly or unjustly MK cannot avoid being scapegoat for Afghan critical economic
                    situation. Abandoned MK camps will stand as monuments of American inefficiency.
                    Arghandab and Kajkai dams would be monuments American ability. Only loan making
                    possible continued MK employment and completion Helmand project can avoid
                    reduced US prestige and cooling of present cordial Afghan-US relations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1233-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1233-f1-content">
                <p>Abdul Majid Khan.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1233-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1233-f2-content">
                <p>Morrison–Knudsen, Afghanistan, an American construction firm working on contract
                    to the Government of Afghanistan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
